}, {"t_ms": 370877, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GGZ5AYxacK6F2RkX5TJstP", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 370877, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GGZ5AYxacK6F2RkX5TJstP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 372846, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. The test expects `2.675 \u2192 2.68` and `2.665 \u2192 2.66`, which only `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` produces.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, \"Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\", targets main. I did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RdqVbGUFEYhk37jqZG9APt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XmZYn8ErpA7DXGDbA1FkGb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016vra28vLnkWpQ2RoT8Mvus", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 (7 is odd, so it goes to the even 8), and 2.665 rounds to 2.66. The bug is that `src/money.py` uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create a branch and make that one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RmjzraosLzt5DAxR8FmHxd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012ZCeHeBfekJQk1KDGSSkgU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money's docstring specifies banker's rounding per FIN-212, but the\nimplementation used ROUND_HALF_UP. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so the\nnightly tests/test_money.py passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The change is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QtdzEFwu4xAJ5aN59m8FBe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Qzpt2d695yc9pNAk5cgEvg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Now I'll open the pull request against main and request alex as reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GGZ5AYxacK6F2RkX5TJstP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build of payments-service fails in `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`. `round_money` is documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212, but it used `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis PR switches `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Examples: `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit 08d3cd5986: passed.\n\nRef: FIN-212", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. The test expects `2.675 \u2192 2.68` and `2.665 \u2192 2.66`, which only `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` produces.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-banker-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, \"Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\", targets main. I did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}